### 4. Visible Faults & Technical Issues

* **Grotesque AI Object Hallucination (The Roast Goose):** At **00:52–00:56**, instead of a plucked roast goose, the AI generated a bizarre hybrid creature: it has a roasted brown body with a carving knife and fork stuck in its back, but it also has a feathered live goose head/neck, webbed feet, and **two creepy eyeballs inside its stuffed body cavity**. It looks like body-horror comedy and completely ruins the tone.
* **Physics / Action Errors:**
  * **00:10:** In the carriage shot, the girl is already barefoot *before* her slipper flies into the air at **00:11**, and the slipper flies up from the middle of the road nowhere near her feet.
  * **00:34–00:35:** The match head spontaneously combusts in mid-air a couple of inches away from the wall without ever scraping the stone.
  * **01:29–01:31:** Instead of striking the bundle of matches against the wall, she strikes a single match against the heads of the other matches in her hand.
* **Audio / Visual Sync Errors:**
  * **00:46:** We hear a loud match-strike sound effect, but on screen the match is already lit in her hand.
  * **00:58:** Again, we hear a match-strike sound effect over a shot where she is already kneeling in front of the giant Christmas tree with no match in sight.
  * **01:21:** A match-strike sound effect plays *after* she was already holding a lit match at **01:20**, right on the cut to the wide shot of Grandmother.
  * **01:50:** The townswoman's line *"She wanted to warm herself"* is spoken while the woman in the foreground is in profile with her mouth closed.
* **Jarring Cuts & Continuity Errors:**
  * **00:56–00:57:** In **00:55**, the girl is sitting on the **left** side of the corner while the goose approaches from the right. As the light dies at **00:56**, the image morphs/dissolves into a shot where the girl is suddenly kneeling on the **right** side of the corner facing left.
  * **01:15:** A pointless, jarring jump cut between two zoomed crops of the exact same still image (**01:11–01:15** and **01:15–01:19**).
* **Subtitle / Pacing Issues:**
  * **00:31–00:37:** The subtitle *"Her hands were numb. If she dared strike just one..."* stays on screen across two shots, lingering for three seconds after the narrator finishes speaking.
  * **01:26–01:29:** In the close-up of the girl crying *"Grandmother! Take me with you!"*, her mouth barely moves in sync with the emotional voice acting.

